{"id": "section-body-14888", "title": "Ophthalmia Neonatorum/Neonatal Conjunctivitis", "chapterId": "chapter-fourteen", "tocLevel": 4, "tocPath": ["APPROACH TO PATIENTS WITH EMERGENCY CONDITIONS", "EYE DISEASES AND REFRACTIVE ERRORS", "Painful Red Eyes", "Ophthalmia Neonatorum/Neonatal Conjunctivitis"], "blocks": [{"id": "body-14888", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Ophthalmia Neonatorum/Neonatal Conjunctivitis", "runs": [{"text": "Ophthalmia"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Neonatorum/Neonatal"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Conjunctivitis"}], "level": 4, "list": {"level": 3, "numberingId": "1271"}}, {"id": "body-14889", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "This is acute bacterial infection of the eyes that affect newborn baby during the first 28days of life. The infection is acquired from mother’s birth canal secretions. It is characterized by inflammation of the conjunctivae, sticky eyes to abundant purulent discharge and eyelids oedema. Causative organisms are Neisseria Gonorrhea, Chlamydia spp and Staphylococcus spp.", "runs": [{"text": "This is acute bacterial infection of the eyes that affect newborn baby during the first 28days of life. The infection is acquired from mother’s birth canal secretions. It is characterized by inflammation of the conjunctivae, sticky eyes to abundant purulent discharge and eyelids oedema. Causative organisms are Neisseria Gonorrhea, Chlamydia spp and Staphylococcus spp."}]}, {"id": "body-14892", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Clinical Presentation", "runs": [{"text": "Clinical"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Presentation"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-14893", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Ranges from mild (small amount of sticky exudates) to severe form (profuse pus and swollen eye lids) depending on the causative organism", "runs": [{"text": "Ranges from mild (small amount of sticky exudates) to severe form (profuse pus and swollen eye lids) depending on the causative "}, {"text": "organism"}], "list": {"level": 4, "numberingId": "1271"}}, {"id": "body-14894", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "There can be rapid ulceration and perforation of corneal which eventually leads to blindness if", "runs": [{"text": "There can be rapid ulceration and perforation of corneal"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "which"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "eventually"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "leads"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "to"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "blindness"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "if"}], "list": {"level": 4, "numberingId": "1271"}}, {"id": "body-14895", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Investigations", "runs": [{"text": "Investigations"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-14896", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Pus swab for Gram Stain", "runs": [{"text": "Pus"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "swab"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "for"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Gram"}, {"text": " Stain"}], "list": {"level": 4, "numberingId": "1271"}}, {"id": "body-14897", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Pus for Culture and sensitivity", "runs": [{"text": "Pus"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "for"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Culture"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "sensitivity"}], "list": {"level": 4, "numberingId": "1271"}}, {"id": "body-14898", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Vaginal swab for Gram stain and culture and sensitivity", "runs": [{"text": "Vaginal"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "swab"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "for"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Gram"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "stain"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "culture"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and "}, {"text": "sensitivity"}], "list": {"level": 4, "numberingId": "1271"}}, {"id": "body-14900", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "treatment is delayed especially in gonorrhea cases.", "runs": [{"text": "treatment"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "is"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "delayed"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "especially"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "in"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "gonorrhea "}, {"text": "cases."}]}, {"id": "body-14901", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "It usually presents 3–4days of life", "runs": [{"text": "It"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "usually"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "presents"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "3–4days"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "life"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1253"}}, {"id": "body-14902", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Late\tand\tmild\tpresentation\tis\tdue\tto Staphylococcus or undefined", "runs": [{"text": "Late"}, {"text": "\t"}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": "\t"}, {"text": "mild"}, {"text": "\t"}, {"text": "presentation"}, {"text": "\t"}, {"text": "is"}, {"text": "\t"}, {"text": "due"}, {"text": "\t"}, {"text": "to "}, {"text": "Staphylococcus or undefined"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1253"}}, {"id": "body-14905", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Maternal VDRL/RPR test should be done, if positive treat as per STI guideline.", "runs": [{"text": "Maternal"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "VDRL/RPR"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "test"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "should"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "be"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "done,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "if positive treat as per STI guideline."}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1253"}}, {"id": "body-14908", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Non-Pharmacological Management", "runs": [{"text": "Non-Pharmacological"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Management"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-14909", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Cleanse or wipe eyes of all newborn babies with a clean cloth, cotton wool or swab, taking care not to touch or injure the eye", "runs": [{"text": "Cleanse"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "or"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "wipe"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "eyes"}, {"tex